[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    560[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // ===========================================================================
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    561[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // Phase C — error / boundary paths (see ERRORS.md).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    562[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    563[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // The C library has NO rejection path: `void driver(float)` has no return
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    564[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // value, no pointer parameter, no enum/flag parameter, no assertion and no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    565[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // range check. The tests below pin down that fact and cover the generic
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    566[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // boundaries in the only forms this API can express them.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    567[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // ===========================================================================
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    568[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    569[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// ERRORS.md B1 — there is no pointer parameter to pass NULL through.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    570[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ///
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    571[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// Asserted structurally: `driver`'s ABI signature takes a single `float` in a
